---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.tsx";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Terms · Hostbeam"
  description="The terms for using and buying Hostbeam, in plain language: what the license grants, how refunds work, and the honest limits of a small software product."
>
  <div class="site" id="top">
    <Nav />
    <main class="wrap" style="max-width: 720px; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 96px">
      <p class="note">Terms of use · last updated 27 September 2026</p>
      <h1 class="h2" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px)">
        Plain terms for a simple product.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 20px">
        Hostbeam is software you run on your own devices, talking to your own servers. These
        terms cover the few things worth writing down. Using or buying Hostbeam means you agree
        with them.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 18px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
        Hostbeam is made and operated by <strong>PunkABeat</strong>, a sole proprietorship, and
        that is the name you will see as the seller on your receipt.
      </p>

      <section style="margin-top: 48px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">Free use</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Hostbeam is free to use for as long as you like, for any purpose, with every feature
          and no account required. On the Mac it asks now and then whether you'd like to buy a
          license; if you keep using it, please do. The iPhone app is free and sells nothing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">The license</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          A Hostbeam license is a one-time purchase for one person. It hides the reminder on up
          to 3 of your Macs and covers every Hostbeam 1 release, with no time limit. A later major
          version (Hostbeam 2) may be a paid, discounted upgrade; until you upgrade, that version
          shows the reminder, and the versions your license covers keep working with every
          feature. Deactivate a Mac in the app to free its seat for another.
          Please don't share or resell keys; that's the one thing that breaks the honest model
          this pricing depends on.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="refunds" style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">Purchases and refunds</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Nothing is sold on this site any more: Hostbeam is free, with every feature and no
          reminder. Licenses were sold until November 2026 by
          <a href="https://paddle.com" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle</a>, the merchant of
          record, under
          <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle's buyer terms</a>;
          a key bought then keeps working. What applies to such a purchase is on the
          <a href="/refunds/" style="color: var(--beam)">refund and cancellation policy</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">The honest limits</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Hostbeam is provided as is. It moves files between machines you control, using access
          you configured; you're responsible for where you point it and what you beam. We work
          hard to make it reliable, but we can't promise it is free of bugs, and to the maximum
          extent the law allows, our liability for any damages is limited to what you paid for
          your license. Nothing here limits rights that consumer law gives you and doesn't let
          us take away.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">Housekeeping</h2>
        <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7">
          Hostbeam is an independent, developer-run product. How we handle data is in the
          <a href="/privacy/" style="color: var(--beam)">privacy policy</a>. If these terms change,
          the date at the top changes with them, and material changes will be called out plainly.
          Questions:
          <a href="mailto:support@hostbeam.app" style="color: var(--beam)">support@hostbeam.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>
